Found defects:

- **Line 266: check that cannot fail / wrapper status code.**  
  Exact input: run `python scripts/apply_review_structural_fixes.py --apply --root F:\tmp\definitely_missing_root`.  
  Consequence: `root.glob("*_REVIEW.html")` scans zero files, reports success, and returns `0`, so a release gate can pass without touching any review file.

- **Line 226: idempotency guard satisfied by marker text, not the live work.**  
  Exact input: one `A_REVIEW.html` containing the literal bytes of `NEW_HE` inside an HTML comment, followed by the literal bytes of `OLD_HE` as the actual live `highlightEvidence` function; run `--apply --root <dir>`.  
  Consequence: `if NEW_HE in text` fires first, so the old live function is left unfixed.

- **Line 237: same marker-text idempotency defect for CT.gov.**  
  Exact input: one `A_REVIEW.html` containing the literal bytes of `NEW_CTGOV` inside an HTML comment, followed by the literal bytes of `OLD_CTGOV` as the actual live `items.push` block; run `--apply --root <dir>`.  
  Consequence: `if NEW_CTGOV in text` fires first, so the old live CT.gov row is left unfixed.

- **Line 213: COULD NOT DETERMINE selector keyed to corpus form.**  
  Missing: the actual caller contract / directory layout for where `*_REVIEW.html` files live; this code only scans direct children of `--root`, not nested files.

No proven defect found in this packet for CRLF/LF text comparison, merged-cell/off-by-one tabulation, zero conflated with absent, or negation dropped.
